From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jfacemyer <1776340+jfacemyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:31:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wineboot: Don't show the wait window when
 WINEBOOT_HIDE_DIALOG is set.

Every prefix update (wineboot -u) and every prefix creation shows the
"The Wine configuration is being updated" window. An installer or
manager that runs the update itself and shows its own progress has no
way to suppress it. With WINEBOOT_HIDE_DIALOG set to anything but "0"
(the variable Proton uses) the window is not shown; unset, nothing
changes.

From neutron-wine (Nico-LaFoucate).
---
 programs/wineboot/wineboot.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
index 7dda9ec..3cfc7c9 100644
--- a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
+++ b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
@@ -1701,7 +1701,9 @@ static void update_wineprefix( BOOL force )
 
         if ((process = start_rundll32( inf_path, L"PreInstall", IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_TARGET_HOST )))
         {
-            HWND hwnd = show_wait_window();
+            /* as in Proton, WINEBOOT_HIDE_DIALOG set (and not "0") means no wait window */
+            const WCHAR *hide = _wgetenv( L"WINEBOOT_HIDE_DIALOG" );
+            HWND hwnd = (hide && *hide && wcscmp( hide, L"0" )) ? NULL : show_wait_window();
             for (;;)
             {
                 if (process)
